  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crisis Specific Appeals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ireland&#x2019;s humanitarian response and funding is directed to where needs are greatest in sudden onset, protracted and conflict related crises, with a particular emphasis on forgotten and underfunded emergencies. Funding is allocated to UN managed Country Based Pooled Funds (CBPFs), ICRC and UN agencies for country specific responses.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Crisis Specific Appeals budget line, Ireland will continue to respond to severe, large scale, humanitarian crises around the globe, in Africa, the Middle East, Asia and Latin America. The CBPFs are country based flexible pooled funds that provide approximately 70% of funding to NGOs, including national and local NGOs. This is well-aligned with Ireland&apos;s Grand Bargain commitment on quality funding and localisation.</narrative>
  </description>
